From: Wisbendji Fimerlus <archledger236@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:16:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] applets/appmenu: name the search action appmenu-guarded
 (Plasma Fusion)

Downstream only. Plasma Fusion's top bar hides the global menu's Search
entry while it is named "appmenu" (the unfixed applet); this build
carries the fix from the previous patch, so the entry stays visible.
Drop this patch together with the previous one.

Signed-off-by: Wisbendji Fimerlus <archledger236@gmail.com>
---
 applets/appmenu/appmenumodel.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/applets/appmenu/appmenumodel.cpp b/applets/appmenu/appmenumodel.cpp
index 3a3678d..9c087b2 100644
--- a/applets/appmenu/appmenumodel.cpp
+++ b/applets/appmenu/appmenumodel.cpp
@@ -83,7 +83,8 @@ AppMenuModel::AppMenuModel(QObject *parent)
     if (KWindowSystem::isPlatformWayland()) {
         m_searchAction = new QAction(this);
         m_searchAction->setText(i18n("Search"));
-        m_searchAction->setObjectName(QStringLiteral("appmenu"));
+        // Plasma Fusion: tells its top bar that the search results are guarded (drop with the fix).
+        m_searchAction->setObjectName(QStringLiteral("appmenu-guarded"));
 
         m_searchMenu.reset(new QMenu);
         auto searchAction = new QWidgetAction(this);
